.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[],"properties":{"securityScore":100,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789176603.0671299,"endTime":1789176621.2146893}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"frontend-arch-analyzer","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5767h5ed458yrz0msn6wg4wp98e90a4-IwJYLA/clawscan-skillspector-433116896/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T01:30:02.004077+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":51,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":260,"executable":false,"size_bytes":12176,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":289,"executable":false,"size_bytes":11801,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"frontend-arch-skill.md","type":"markdown","lines":539,"executable":false,"size_bytes":17006,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-dc4e839443c4412a90a3149e4cf32f3b","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"frontend-arch-skill.md","start_line":207,"end_line":null},"finding":".env ","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"| Tree-shaking | 2 分 | sideEffects 配置正确 |\n| 路径别名 | 1 分 | @ 或 ~ 别名配置 |\n| Source Map | 1 分 | 生产环境关闭或使用 hidden-source-map |\n| 环境变量 | 1 分 | .env 文件 + cross-env / dotenv |\n| 缓存策略 | 1 分 | contenthash 文件名 |\n\n**Vite 项目检查清单：**","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"66ef81c27c03406fd9935e5fc86fc4126d7150c15b8d076fdc528d05cea7c7bf","occurrences":[{"file":"frontend-arch-skill.md","start_line":207,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-dc4e839443c4412a90a3149e4cf32f3b","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"frontend-arch-skill.md","start_line":219,"end_line":null},"finding":".env ","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"| Tree-shaking | 2 分 | sideEffects 配置正确 |\n| 路径别名 | 1 分 | @ 或 ~ 别名配置 |\n| Source Map | 1 分 | 生产环境关闭或使用 hidden-source-map |\n| 环境变量 | 1 分 | .env 文件 + cross-env / dotenv |\n| 缓存策略 | 1 分 | contenthash 文件名 |\n\n**Vite 项目检查清单：**","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"66ef81c27c03406fd9935e5fc86fc4126d7150c15b8d076fdc528d05cea7c7bf","occurrences":[{"file":"frontend-arch-skill.md","start_line":219,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-5055c23742de4e8e88cb78147463e72f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":67,"end_line":69},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger phrase list includes generic terms such as component design, build config, and monorepo that may appear in ordinary conversation or unrelated review requests, causing the skill to activate when the user did not explicitly ask for this architecture-analysis behavior. In a prompt-based skill system, over-broad activation can unexpectedly inject long instruction sets and alter assistant behavior, which is a real prompt-routing security and safety issue even without code execution.","remediation":"Narrow activation phrases to explicit, high-intent combinations such as 'analyze frontend architecture' or '前端架构分析', require project-analysis context before activation, and add disambiguation/confirmation for ambiguous terms like 'monorepo' or '组件设计'. Prefer multi-factor routing that combines keywords with intent classification instead of single-term matching.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":67,"end_line":69}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-55a0248bc5e2494db3bab1a6bbf7a9fa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":60,"end_line":79},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation keywords are very broad and include common frontend terms like webpack, vite, monorepo, and component design. This can cause the skill to activate in conversations that only mention these topics casually, leading to unintended prompt takeover, irrelevant architectural judgments, or disclosure requests for project structure/configuration beyond what the user intended.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger list to higher-precision phrases that explicitly request architecture analysis, such as 'analyze architecture', 'review project structure', or 'frontend architecture audit'. Add negative conditions and disambiguation logic so the skill activates only when the user clearly asks for an architecture review rather than mentioning a tool or topic in passing.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":60,"end_line":79}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-2cfaaa4cdbb9433eb669ec20484f6b0d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":83,"end_line":85},"finding":null,"explanation":"The intent-based activation rules are underspecified and rely on subjective interpretation of whether a user is asking if a choice is 'reasonable' or 'how to optimize'. In an agent system, ambiguous boundaries increase the chance of misrouting, causing the skill to engage when the user wanted a narrow answer and potentially steering the interaction into broad project analysis or unnecessary data collection.","remediation":"Define explicit activation thresholds and exclusions, such as requiring both project context and an explicit request for review/audit/assessment. Add examples of non-activation cases, and require a brief confirmation step when signals are ambiguous before the skill starts a full architecture evaluation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":83,"end_line":85}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-8032b85254f946d78d86610681d10f0b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"frontend-arch-skill.md","start_line":1,"end_line":1},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill content is entirely written as a Chinese-only rule engine and its output templates, prompts, and follow-up guidance all assume Chinese responses without offering a language fallback or stating a justified locale restriction. In a general-purpose agent skill, this can cause user intent mismatch, reduce transparency, and create unsafe interaction failures when users cannot understand requests for sensitive project data or remediation advice.","remediation":"Add an explicit language-negotiation rule at the top of the skill, such as responding in the user's language by default and using Chinese only when the user requests it. If the skill is intentionally Chinese-only, document that restriction clearly in metadata and require the skill to refuse activation or provide a short localized notice when the user's language does not match.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"frontend-arch-skill.md","start_line":1,"end_line":1}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c1d86b70251d4216858b5dee19eb9fb9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document presents the skill primarily in Chinese, with only a brief English subtitle, and does not clarify whether outputs or interaction language follow the user's preference. Because locale and language behavior are part of policy scope, the absence of an explicit user-choice statement creates a risk that the skill may default to a specific language without opt-in.","remediation":"Add a short language policy statement indicating that the skill should respond in the user's preferred language or ask for language preference when unclear. If the skill is intended for Chinese-speaking users only, document that limitation explicitly and justify it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-59af0748eec04c51ad6d4c255e76fa58","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.76,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document title, metadata, and most operating instructions are in Chinese, which can imply a default language behavior without explicit user opt-in. Although English trigger examples are included, the file does not clearly state that output language will follow user preference or that users may choose their locale.","remediation":"Add a brief policy statement near the top saying the skill should respond in the user's preferred language or match the user's input language, with explicit support for both Chinese and English.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":22}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer